    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Bit manipulation</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Popcount</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-1-bits/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 191</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Number of 1 Bits</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Count the set bits of an integer. Shifting and testing each of the 32 bits works; the interview answer is Kernighan's trick <code>n &amp;= n - 1</code>, which deletes the lowest 1 per turn and so loops once per set bit. The follow-up (\"called many times\") is a lookup table or the hardware popcount.</p>\n"
  },
